980	 * Regression test for the double-free reported against ZipArchive::close() when an
981	 * archive opened with fromWritableBuffer is modified and closed (double_free_report.pdf).
982	 *
983	 * close() must read the rewritten archive back into a freshly allocated buffer instead
984	 * of reusing/realloc'ing the very buffer that backs the libzip source. The crafted input
985	 * below makes the rewrite exceed the original buffer length, which forces the buffer to
986	 * grow inside close() - the exact path that used to free the source-backed buffer twice.
987	 *
988	 * Under AddressSanitizer/valgrind (see the Makefile tests targets), a regression would
989	 * surface as a double-free / invalid-free here.
990	 */
